# Test: show bgp rib protocol and request bgp rib fastpath state their arguments
# VALIDATES: each usage line carries the argument the model declares, so the
#            protocol name and the three fastpath words are read from the
#            model rather than from the summary sentence
# PREVENTS: a grammar spelled in the summary, where `<protocol>` is inline
#           HTML under CommonMark and vanishes from the published reference
#           (plan/journal/command-takes-an-untyped-positional-value.md,
#           2026-09-15)
#
# The line each command states is the one the MODEL renders
# (internal/component/bgp/plugins/cmd/rib/yang/ze-rib-cmd.yang). The summary
# is rejected where it used to spell the grammar, so a reader of the help page
# meets each token once.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze show bgp rib protocol help
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=ze show bgp rib protocol <protocol>
reject=stderr:pattern=\[peer-selector\]
reject=stderr:pattern=\[pipeline-args

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze request bgp rib fastpath help
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=ze request bgp rib fastpath <enable|disable|status>
reject=stderr:pattern=fast path \(rib-arch-6\): <
